From 0d5267279a7ad21b9deeb5d2a8123396077cba82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yuji mitobe <mitobex7@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 09:03:42 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] ASoC: qcom: q6asm: validate WRITE_DONE token before
 buffer access

The DSP echoes the token of the completed write command in the APR
header. The token is masked down to its 16-bit index field but never
checked against the number of mapped periods, so a bogus or corrupted
response indexes outside the port buffer array.

Mirror the READ_DONE validation and reject out-of-range tokens instead
of dereferencing an invalid buffer.

Signed-off-by: yuji mitobe <mitobex7@gmail.com>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm.c
index 7c96f8d83b38e..5199381f48052 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm.c
@@ -698,6 +698,14 @@ static int32_t q6asm_stream_callback(struct apr_device *adev,
 				goto done;
 			}
 
+			if (token >= port->num_periods) {
+				dev_err(ac->dev,
+					"WRITE_DONE token %u out of range %u\n",
+					token, port->num_periods);
+				ret = -EINVAL;
+				goto done;
+			}
+
 			phys = port->buf[token].phys;
 
 			if (lower_32_bits(phys) != result->opcode ||
